---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base
  title="Standards"
  description="The rules every piece on this site is held to, and how to check them."
  ogSlug="standards"
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Standards</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The rules every piece here is held to. They are published so a reader can
      hold the writing to them.
    </p>

    <h2>Every checkable claim carries a live link</h2>
    <p>
      A number or an attributed statement travels with a named source and a
      working link to it, or it does not run. Links are rendered plainly in the
      text, marked where they leave the site, so a claim can be followed without
      hunting for a footnote.
    </p>

    <h2>Sources are named, not gestured at</h2>
    <p>
      "Research shows" is not a source. The organisation, the document and the
      date belong in the text.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections stay visible</h2>
    <p>
      When a piece changes after publication, the change is dated on the piece
      rather than made quietly.
    </p>

    <p class="note">
      This page is a first cut, published so the standard is on the record from
      day one. It expands with the content build; the rules above are already
      in force. Pieces held to them are on{' '}
      <a href={href('/writing')}>Writing</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
